WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.200
-Guys, since we're back at home,

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.200
I thought it would be fun
to do another installment

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.200
of "Ask the Fallons."

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.100
This where my wife Nancy and I

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.901
answer questions
that you guys send in.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:10.834
It could be about us or the kids
or life or anything.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:13.534
So here's another
"Ask the Fallons."

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:17.868
-♪ Ask the Fallons,
Ask the Fallons ♪

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:19.601
-Okay.
Well, we're back.

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.968
-Yeah.
-It's been one year. [ Laughs ]

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.934
-It's been a year.
-I thought I was out.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.033
[ Laughs ]

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:30.534
I totally did
my civic showbiz duty.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:33.100
-Honey.
-And yet here I am again.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.534
-Did I publicly thank you?

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.467
-A year later in the same coat.
-I don't know if I did.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:38.434
-Alright, we have
a bunch of questions

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:40.434
from everyone
who watches the show.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:43.501
And people really like this bit
that we did

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:45.534
where it's us just walking
around and talking.

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:46.434
Alright. Here's one of these.

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:47.901
This is interesting.
-Okay.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:50.567
-Who said "I love you" first?
Where and when did it happen?

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:52.701
Do you want to plug your ears
and I'll tell my version?

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:56.133
-No, no. Oh, yeah. I wonder
if our version is the same.

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:58.200
-We kind of do this
on the show with other --

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.501
So maybe plug your ears,
and I'll say it real quick.

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:01.834
-Okay.
-And maybe hum something.

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.200
-Oh, I see.
♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.667
-Alright, I said "I love you"
in London.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:09.367
We were a press thing
for "Fever Pitch."

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.701
Nancy's a producer.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.801
We just would hang out in
the hotel all the time,

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:15.701
listen to music, Harry Nelson,
Randy Newman.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.868
And I put on "Taxi," which is
my favorite show.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.767
-New fence!
-And I made her watch this show

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:24.367
about their dreams or something,
and it was just good.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.234
And then we kissed.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.801
We were in my hotel room,
we kissed for the first time,

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:31.734
and it was honestly

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:34.501
the best kiss I've ever had
in my life.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:37.801
And I think I said
"I love you" after that.

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:40.701
Alright. That's my story.
Honey, I'm done.

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:42.400
[ Clears throat ] I'm done, hon.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.601
-Okay.
-Alright.

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:46.334
Who said --
-Who said "I love you"? He did.

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:53.000
And we had been having big
crushes on each other

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.734
during "Fever Pitch."

00:01:54.734 --> 00:02:00.667
And like two awesome nerds,
we didn't do anything about it

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:03.734
but flirt a lot and listen to
a lot of music

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:05.667
and say, like, good night
at 4:00 in the morning

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.868
like total nerd balls.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:11.033
-I'm a pretty smooth dude.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.367
-Okay.

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:16.868
So we wrapped the movie,
"Fever Pitch,"

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:21.601
and we were going to London
to sell it,

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:24.467
and we went out
one really fun night

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:28.667
and, um, we ended up -- -
-Halloween, wasn't it?

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:31.367
-No, that was in London.
That was our first kiss.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:34.534
But our first "I love you"
was in London.

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:36.234
And I had to leave the next day.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:37.901
I was there for the press
junket, and then I had to leave,

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:39.434
and I think you all
were going somewhere.

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:43.767
But that night, he said,
"I love you.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:44.868
I'm in love with you."

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.400
And I don't even know
if I said it back

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.701
because I think you knew
that I loved you.

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:52.200
So I think that then --
-Wow.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.367
-Well, maybe I did, but I don't
think it was like,

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:56.033
"I love you, I love you,
I love you."

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:57.901
You were like, "I love you."

00:02:57.901 --> 00:03:00.701
And then I flew home
the next day,

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:02.567
and I will never forget
that flight.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:05.567
I had to go back to California.

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:10.133
And you know that feeling when
you're just smiling ear to ear

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:12.334
and it's just the best feeling
in the world

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.901
when you, like, love someone
and they love you

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:17.267
and you have a crush
and it's reciprocated?

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:19.434
And...that's my memory.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:21.000
And then I feel like
from there --

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.467
-I told the wrong story.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:26.000
-I thought it was first kiss.
I confused the two.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.167
-[ Gasps ] Oh, no.
First kiss, Boston.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:32.367
Yeah. Oh! When we levitated?

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:33.467
-That was a good kiss.

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:35.734
-That was the best kiss
I've ever had.

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:38.901
So that was two stories --
an "I love you" --

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:40.334
-Yeah. You got two stories
out of that one.

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:42.701
-Yeah. And yeah.

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.801
-I don't know what story
you got.

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.033
That was the "I love you" story.

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.667
[ Geese honking ]

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.067
-Hi, guys.

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:52.200
-Wow.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.400
-I just wanted to thank you
for doing these walks and talks.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.300
And I want to thank everyone
who's watching for enjoying --

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.701
-Yeah.
We should really thank them.

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:00.968
[ Laughs ]

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:02.934
-Yeah.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:04.167
Really.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.300
This is -- it's been fun.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.367
-It has been fun.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:11.200
A little glimpse into...

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.000
-Yeah.
-...Jimmy and his wife.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.934
-Love you, cutie.
-I love you.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:18.868
You're welcome.
-Alright, do you want another?

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:20.667
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:22.033
Did you throw in a little
"You're welcome" there?

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.634
-Yeah! Just said,
"You're welcome."

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:25.767
-That's what she does
every time we kiss.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:28.801
She says, "You're welcome."
-No! You said thank you.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.868
[ Laughs ]
That would be so good.

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:33.300
-That's the way
our relationship is.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.667
-Oh, my God.
You're welcome.

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.501
"Honey, I love you."
"You're welcome."

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.133
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:40.033
-Alright, you want to do
another question?

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:41.167
-Yeah.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:42.934
-What's your go-to recipe
for a night in?

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.434
Ready? One, two, three.

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:45.567
-Takeout.
-Takeout.

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:47.400
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.767
Did Nancy's family
accept Jimmy immediately?

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:52.067
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:54.801
No, no. Of course.
I'm laughing.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:58.667
-I didn't get to the end.
-Our New Hampshire weekend.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.934
-It was honestly --

00:05:00.934 --> 00:05:02.734
-We had a "meet the parents"
weekend.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:07.267
-My parents came to visit
Nancy's parents

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:09.300
for the first time
in New Hampshire.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.634
-It was the first meeting
of everybody.

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:12.200
-Couldn't have been
a bigger disaster.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.100
-We decided not to do a dinner.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.767
"Why don't we do
an entire weekend together?"

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:19.000
[ Laughs ]

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.167
Because what could
go wrong there?

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:22.868
There's not a story
that could go wrong.

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:26.067
-The night before, my mother
calls me and she goes,

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:28.067
"Jimmy, don't hang up."

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:30.133
That's the signal for,

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.133
"You're gonna get angry
at what I'm about to say."

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:34.167
I go, "What do you mean?
Hi, Mom. How are you?

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.467
First of all, hi."

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.767
"Alright, don't hang up."
I go, "I heard you."

00:05:37.767 --> 00:05:40.734
She goes,
"Mm-kay, not a big deal,

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:42.934
but Daddy's tooth

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:46.434
fell out today," or last night
or something.

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:47.901
"His front tooth fell out."

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:49.334
I go, "His front tooth?"

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:51.434
-Front. Not a back or anything
that you could hide.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.300
-I go, "Go to the dentist.
Get a cap or get something."

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.300
She goes, "The dentist
is on vacation."

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:58.801
I go, "This is a di--
You can't come meet --

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:01.000
This is Nancy's family.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.634
You can't meet them
with no teeth."

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:07.200
She goes, "It's fine.
Daddy's just not gonna smile."

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.133
-He just won't smile.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:10.834
-"Not gonna smile?
What are you talking about?

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:12.367
This is a weekend."

00:06:12.367 --> 00:06:15.701
I go, "I'm hanging up,"
I was that mad.

00:06:15.701 --> 00:06:18.167
She goes, "Well, don't hang up.
Wait, wait, one more thing.

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:20.467
I rubbed my eye
in my sleep last night,

00:06:20.467 --> 00:06:21.801
and I have a bloody eye."

00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:25.300
I go,
"You've got to be kidding me."

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:29.667
So here, meet my parents,
a pirate and a Jack-O-Lantern.

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:31.367
-Yeah.
-My mom would be laughing.

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:33.234
She would be laughing.
-Oh, she would be laughing so --

00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:35.100
Are you kidding?
This is the best story ever.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.634
-Exactly. She loved it.

00:06:36.634 --> 00:06:40.801
So, it was probably
April, March.

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:43.300
It was --
The lake was just done --

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:47.267
-The ice was out,
but it was very cold.

00:06:47.267 --> 00:06:50.634
-My dad goes, "I'm gonna jump
in the lake," to be funny.

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:52.033
-Yeah.
-Anyway, so we go,

00:06:52.033 --> 00:06:54.234
"Alright, let's get ready.
We're gonna go out to dinner."

00:06:54.234 --> 00:06:56.667
So we're getting ready
to go out for dinner.

00:06:56.667 --> 00:07:00.434
Mind you, my mom had bad knees,
and she could --

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:03.667
-Kind of not bend ankle or knee,
really, in a way.

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:05.601
-I don't know if her knee's bad
or her ankles.

00:07:05.601 --> 00:07:10.434
Nothing quite -- It was very
interesting, how she walked.

00:07:10.434 --> 00:07:14.434
So anyways, we were upstairs,
getting ready for dinner,

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:18.334
and there's a knock on the door
where we were getting ready,

00:07:18.334 --> 00:07:20.701
and I go, "It can't be.

00:07:20.701 --> 00:07:22.501
It can't be my mom because" --

00:07:22.501 --> 00:07:24.100
-She couldn't get up
those stairs, right?

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.501
-There's no way.

00:07:25.501 --> 00:07:28.200
So she comes up the stairs,
and we kind of smell smoke.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.734
-Uh-huh. As we open the door,
we smell.

00:07:30.734 --> 00:07:32.334
-We open the door, smell smoke,
she goes,

00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:35.400
"Everything's fine."
-"Don't worry."

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.534
-"Everything's fine."

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:40.868
I go, "What's going on?
What's happening?"

00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:46.367
She goes, "Daddy jumped in
the lake with all his money."

00:07:46.367 --> 00:07:47.734
-A wad of...

00:07:47.734 --> 00:07:49.634
-20s.
-...I don't know, fives?

00:07:49.634 --> 00:07:54.000
-$20 bills. I think it was $500,
maybe, or $200.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:58.934
-Just a wad.
-$500 of $20 bills.

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:00.868
She goes,
"And so his money got wet."

00:08:00.868 --> 00:08:03.634
And so he tried
to dry his money.

00:08:03.634 --> 00:08:06.601
My dad put $500
in the microwave...

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:07.868
-In our microwave.

00:08:07.868 --> 00:08:10.367
-..and lit the money on fire.

00:08:10.367 --> 00:08:13.300
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.133
This is one story.

00:08:15.133 --> 00:08:18.601
-And this is just a reminder.
-An old lake house.

00:08:18.601 --> 00:08:20.234
-The old family --

00:08:20.234 --> 00:08:24.601
It's not valuable, but it is
invaluable to the hearts.

00:08:24.601 --> 00:08:26.534
[ Laughs ]

00:08:26.534 --> 00:08:30.367
-I go down, there's $20 bills
laid all over the kitchen

00:08:30.367 --> 00:08:32.133
with brown burnt spots.

00:08:32.133 --> 00:08:33.634
I go, "Dad, what --"

00:08:33.634 --> 00:08:36.100
He's like, "I didn't realize,

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.601
I thought you could
dry the money."

00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:39.200
I go...

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:42.133
There's metal in $20 bills,
apparently, like a strip.

00:08:42.133 --> 00:08:45.334
-Just FYI -- don't put money
in the microwave.

00:08:45.334 --> 00:08:47.000
-Honey, that's one story, but --

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.400
-That was one of a few.
-You still married me.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.100
-Yes, we weren't married,
were we?

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.834
Yeah, no, that's -- Aww!
-You're so lucky.

00:08:52.834 --> 00:08:55.033
-I'm so lucky.
-Mwah! You're welcome.

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:56.033
Mwah! You're welcome.

00:08:56.033 --> 00:08:58.734
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:58.734 --> 00:09:00.901
Mwah! You're welcome.
-Mwah! You are welcome, honey.

00:09:01.901 --> 00:09:03.634
-Thank you so much
for those questions, you guys.

